.\" Manual page for parkett. @VERSION@ is filled in by build-deb.sh.
.\"
.\" Author: David M. Anderson
.\" Built with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)
.TH PARKETT 1 "2026\-10\-24" "parkett @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
parkett \- view Apache Parquet files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B parkett
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Parkett
opens an Apache Parquet file as a grid of its rows and, on request, a panel
describing the file itself: its schema, row groups, and each column's codec,
encodings, sizes and statistics. It reads the stretch of the file in view and
nothing more, so a file of millions of rows opens at once.
.PP
It never writes Parquet and never changes the file it opened. A selection
copies to the clipboard as tab\-separated rows, and File, Export as CSV writes
every row, or the columns selected, to a new file.
.SH OPTIONS
There are none.
.B parkett
is a window rather than a command\-line interface.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I file
A Parquet file to open. Without one, the window opens empty.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POTEXT_LANG
The language to show, overriding the desktop's, such as
.BR de .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns success when the window has been closed. A non\-zero status means the
window could not be created at all: no display, or no usable graphics driver.
.SH SEE ALSO
The design of this application is DESIGN.md in its repository at
https://github.com/excelano/parkett.
.SH AUTHOR
David M. Anderson
